# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Silicon Strait — GWW3 Symbolic Logic predicate set
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# Day-7 (2026-05-07) S8 established the four-player frame
# (US_Exec, US_Leg, PRC, ROC) and the deterministic skeleton:
# substrate-protection gate, Davidson-window time-gate, Caucus-density
# derivative, S6 nuclear non-commitment, PRC counter-framing pattern,
# equilibrium-tilt aggregator. Stochastic extensions deferred under
# q1_gww3_documentation (still open since 2026-04-30).
#
# Day-8 (2026-05-12) S6 — this file — promotes the frame in three ways
# and authors fourteen ROC-player predicates plus one cross-player
# promotion of the US_Exec node:
#
#   1. Player promotion: ROC → composite (ROC_Exec, ROC_Leg) with a
#      deterministic gating relation. Frame is now five players.
#   2. Action-node promotion: US_Exec moves from single-action
#      (extend_security_umbrella) to multi-action — adding
#      us_exec_fms_loa_cadence(t) as a continuous-control parameter.
#      Required by S4's ratified-but-pending special-budget Tranche-2
#      (NT$480B contingent on US-FMS-LOA-Round-2).
#   3. Substrate extension: the deterrence-doctrine substrate set
#      grows from three layers (political-constitutional, rhetorical,
#      defense-architectural) to four (adds energy-security via Lai's
#      2026-03 nuclear-restart pivot).
#
# Grammar reference: hassaleh/src/hassaleh/engine/gsl_ops.lark v1.2
# (deterministic subset of GSL). Stochastic extensions are not valid
# GSL and are kept in a dedicated pseudocode block at the bottom of
# this file, marked explicitly. They will become valid once the GWW3
# stochastic runtime grammar lands.
#
# Citations: every load-bearing predicate references the publication
# source(s) by [#N] from publications/2026-05-12-en.md.
#
# Parse-status (Day-9 06:00 fire, 2026-05-16):
#   - Syntactic-conversion pass applied: // comments → #, AND/OR/NOT
#     → lowercase, multi-line IF-AND continuations collapsed.
#   - 12 of 15 predicates + P12-bis parse cleanly under gsl_ops.lark v1.2.
#   - P6, P9, P13 hit grammar gaps (struct kwargs; aggregator-over-
#     comprehension). Refactor pending — see research/audit/parse-verify-
#     2026-05-16.md for the analysis and the two structural options.

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Player frame (5 players, promoted from Day-7 S8)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# PLAYER DECLARATION — documentary, expressed via game_state nodes:
#   US_Exec, US_Leg, PRC, ROC_Exec, ROC_Leg
#
# Day-7 S8's ROC node is replaced by ROC_Exec ⊕ ROC_Leg with a
# deterministic gating relation. The gate's input is a stochastic
# factional-balance term inside ROC_Leg (see kmt_caucus_position
# predicate below). Choosing a flat 5-player frame over a recursive
# ROC sub-game keeps the equilibrium computation tractable while
# preserving the political-economy reality (the factional bargaining
# noise sits inside one player's state, not in a sub-game tree).

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# S1 — ROC_Exec doctrinal predicates [#1, #2, #3, #4, #23]
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ── P1. roc_executive_not_subordinate_assertion ────────────────────────────
# Deterministic. Active since 2024-05-20. Source [#1] (inaugural).
# Reaffirmed implicitly in every subsequent Lai speech-act; explicitly
# extended to "alarming military ambitions" by 2026 NY [#2] and to
# 3%/5% GDP defense pledges by 2025 National Day [#4].
# Encodes the appeasement-equilibrium foreclosure proof embedded in
# the inaugural's "even if we accept ... ambition will not disappear".
MATCH (e:Executive_Speech_Act {actor: "ROC_Exec"}):
    IF e.date >= "2024-05-20" and e.contains_assertion == "not_subordinate":
        game_state.roc_sovereignty_position = "non_subordinate_to_PRC"
        game_state.appeasement_equilibrium_foreclosed = true
        LOG "P1 active: roc_executive_not_subordinate_assertion" LEVEL "info"

# ── P2. roc_legislative_constraint_on_executive_pkg ────────────────────────
# Deterministic gate. Active since DPP became LY minority post-2024.
# Source [#2] (NY plea) + [#3] (EPPD plea) — both speech-acts plead
# for ratification, doubling the gate across defense and tariff packages.
# Stays in effect until a re-election rebalances LY composition.
MATCH (p:Executive_Package {actor: "ROC_Exec"}):
    IF p.type in ["defense_special_budget", "us_tariff_agreement"]:
        IF game_state.dpp_seat_share < 0.5:
            p.passage_gated_by = "kmt_tpp_cooperation"
            p.ratification_class = "joint_output_of_three_gates"
            LOG "P2 gate engaged on executive package" LEVEL "info"

# ── P3. roc_threat_perception_state(prc_military) ──────────────────────────
# Stochastic from 2026-01-01 — encoded as deterministic shell here.
# The 2026 NY shift from "renounce force" (request) to "alarming
# ambitions" (threat-coding) is the regime change. Source [#2].
# Regression possible under (i) 2028 ROC executive transition or # (ii) major PRC de-escalation event. See STOCHASTIC block.
MATCH (s:ROC_Exec_Threat_Coding):
    IF s.date >= "2026-01-01":
        IF s.rhetoric_register == "alarming_military_ambitions":
            game_state.roc_threat_perception_state = "escalating"
            LOG "P3 shell deterministic; regression term is stochastic" LEVEL "info"

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# S2 — KMT opposition / ROC_Leg predicates [#6, #7, #8, #9]
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ── P4. kmt_doctrinal_alignment_with_ccp_92_consensus ──────────────────────
# Deterministic. Operative since 2026-02-03 Beijing forum under Chair
# Cheng Li-wun, institutionalized via Joint Declarations [#6, #7].
# Repudiation path: new chair election or formal Joint-Declarations
# withdrawal. MAC counter-framing [#8] is logged but does not move P4.
MATCH (k:Party {name: "KMT"}):
    IF k.chair == "Cheng_Li_wun" and k.joint_declarations_with_ccp != null and k.joint_declarations_date >= "2026-02-03":
        k.doctrinal_alignment_with_ccp = "1992_consensus"
        k.repudiation_path = "new_chair_election_or_joint_decl_withdrawal"
        game_state.kmt_doctrinal_alignment_active = true

# ── P5. kmt_caucus_position_on_special_defense_budget ──────────────────────
# Stochastic over factional balance — deterministic shell of the
# post-2026-05-08 ratified state. Pre-ratification factional axes:
# NT$380B+N official caucus (Cheng / Fu / Chi); NT$800B Han / Hsu;
# Huang-Fuhsing expulsion pressure. Source [#9, #14, #15].
# Stochastic events that move this: cross-party negotiation outcomes;
# caucus-discipline actions; chair-level transitions.
MATCH (c:Caucus {party: "KMT"}):
    IF c.snapshot_date >= "2026-05-08":
        # Ratified compromise locked the post-passage factional weight.
        c.dominant_position = "NT$780B_three_hundred_unconditional_four_eighty_loa_gated"
        c.pre_passage_factions = ["NT$380B+N", "NT$800B_Han_Hsu", "Huang_Fuhsing"]
        LOG "P5 stochastic; current shell anchored on 2026-05-08 ratification" LEVEL "info"

# ── P6. roc_leg_ratification_signal_to_us ──────────────────────────────────
# Gated coupling. Couples P5 (KMT caucus factional balance) to the
# DPP executive package proposal under P2. The output is the signal
# observed by US_Exec when deciding FMS-LOA cadence (P12-bis below).
# Source: [#3] EPPD legislative-ratification plea + [#9] cross-party
# negotiation pattern + [#15] post-passage NT$780B/300+480 structure.
MATCH (r:ROC_Leg_Ratification):
    IF r.target == "us_arms_procurement" and r.dpp_proposal != null:
        LET p5_state = game_state.kmt_caucus_position
        LET p4_state = game_state.kmt_doctrinal_alignment_active
        # q8(A) hoist: struct(key: value) kwargs not in gsl_ops.lark v1.2
        # (Finding 4, parse-verify-2026-05-16). Compound-state grouping
        # under r.signal_to_us_exec replaced with five flat properties.
        # Grammar-extension (Finding 4(c)) tracked separately as q9.
        r.signal_ratified_amount = r.headline_amount
        r.signal_unconditional_fraction = r.unconditional_amount / r.headline_amount
        r.signal_us_loa_gated_fraction = r.loa_conditional_amount / r.headline_amount
        r.signal_kmt_caucus_dominant = p5_state
        r.signal_kmt_doctrinal_92consensus = p4_state
        SUBMIT_INTENT "update_us_exec_fms_cadence_input" ON game_state

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# S3 — Public opinion / ROC public substrate predicates [#10, #11, #12]
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ── P7. roc_identity_drift_rate ≈ 0 within band(0.62, 0.78) ────────────────
# Deterministic. NCCU 62% (gold standard) ≤ "Taiwanese only" ≤ TPOF 78%.
# σ < 1 pp over 4 years (2022–2025). Source [#10, #11, #12].
# Encodes: identity is not a decision-relevant stochastic variable on
# any horizon the four-player game evaluates over. Identity → party
# correlation is path-stable, not path-dependent.
MATCH (id:ROC_Identity_TimeSeries):
    IF id.taiwanese_only_share_nccu >= 0.62 and id.taiwanese_only_share_tpof <= 0.78 and id.sigma_4yr < 0.01:
        game_state.roc_identity_mobility = "non_mobile_on_decision_horizons"
        game_state.identity_is_decision_variable = false

# ── P8. roc_executive_approval_volatility ──────────────────────────────────
# Stochastic σ ≈ 7.4 pp over 8 waves — deterministic shell of the
# post-2025-10 → post-2025-12 +8.5pp recovery observation.
# Source [#11]. Encodes: ROC_Exec operates in a high-noise approval
# substrate that compresses the window of unconstrained executive
# action; doctrinal moves CAN recover approval (cf. Oct→Dec 2025
# post-National-Day bounce), but the noise floor is structural.
MATCH (a:TPOF_Approval_Wave {subject: "Lai"}):
    IF a.wave_count >= 8 and a.sigma_8wave >= 0.05:
        game_state.roc_exec_approval_substrate = "high_noise"
        game_state.unconstrained_exec_action_window = "compressed_by_noise_floor"
        LOG "P8 stochastic; sigma stable across 2024-2025 wave history" LEVEL "info"

# ── P9. roc_public_us_reliability_perception ───────────────────────────────
# Deterministic split. Source [#11] Oct-2025 TPOF wave:
#   US capable_pct = 0.453   /  US willing_pct = 1 - 0.448 = 0.552
# The split is the most diagnostic single number in the dataset for
# the US-coalition-management dimension. Encodes: any GWW3 model that
# treats US-Taiwan alignment as a single coupling parameter is
# under-determined; the parameter MUST decompose into capability and # willingness terms.
MATCH (p:TPOF_Poll {wave: "2025-10"}):
    IF p.us_capable_pct == 0.453 and p.us_unwilling_pct == 0.448:
        # q8(A) hoist: struct(key: value) kwargs not in gsl_ops.lark v1.2
        # (Finding 4, parse-verify-2026-05-16). Compound-state grouping
        # under game_state.roc_public_us_reliability replaced with two
        # flat properties. Grammar-extension tracked as q9.
        game_state.roc_public_us_reliability_capability = 0.453
        game_state.roc_public_us_reliability_willingness = 0.552
        game_state.us_taiwan_coupling_decomposed = true

# ── P9-bis. roc_public_threat_anchor [PROVISIONAL] ────────────────────────
# Provisional single-wave datapoint: 0.448 plurality attributes
# cross-strait tension to PRC (Oct-2025 TPOF wave). Source [#11].
# PROMOTION to deterministic-multi-wave is gated on recovery of the
# TPOF 12-month war-likelihood image-embedded table (currently a
# Day-8 residual research-gap — q on tomorrow list).
MATCH (p:TPOF_Poll {wave: "2025-10"}):
    IF p.prc_attribution_pct == 0.448:
        game_state.roc_public_threat_anchor_provisional = 0.448
        LOG "P9-bis PROVISIONAL — single wave; multi-wave promotion pending" LEVEL "warn"

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# S4 — Defense reform / ROC_Leg ratification predicates [#13, #14, #15,
#                                                        #16, #17, #18,
#                                                        #19, #20, #21]
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ── P10. roc_defense_spend_structure :: three_layer ────────────────────────
# Deterministic. Source [#17] (Ma Wen-chun decomposition) + [#19]
# (post-passage promulgation). FY2026 total = baseline + supplemental
# + special, with special-budget further decomposed into unconditional
# + US-LOA-gated. Encodes: ROC defense allocation is not a single
# executive-authored number; it is a three-channel flow with three
# distinct authorization gates, and the special channel has an
# internal sub-gate tied to a non-ROC actor (US_Exec).
MATCH (s:ROC_Defense_Spend {fy: "2026"}):
    LET baseline_NTD_B = 949.5
    LET supplemental_NTD_B = 110.0
    LET special_unconditional_NTD_B = 300.0
    LET special_loa_gated_NTD_B = 480.0
    LET total_NTD_B = baseline_NTD_B + supplemental_NTD_B + special_unconditional_NTD_B + special_loa_gated_NTD_B
    s.total_authorized_NTD_B = total_NTD_B
    s.us_loa_gated_fraction = special_loa_gated_NTD_B / total_NTD_B
    s.structure_class = "three_layer_with_sub_gate"

# ── P11. roc_doctrinal_posture :: institutionalized_asymmetric ─────────────
# Deterministic. Source [#16] QDR 2025. Three institutional substrates:
# Littoral Strike Group (force-structure); drone training center
# (training pipeline); drone+MANPADS conscription curriculum
# (conscript-pipeline). Encodes: the doctrinal substrate the ratified
# spend funds is no longer a planning aspiration — it is a
# force-structure-and-pipeline state. Reversal requires explicit
# doctrinal counter-authorship, not just budget redirection.
MATCH (q:QDR {year: 2025}):
    IF q.littoral_strike_group == true and q.drone_training_center == true and q.conscription_drone_curriculum == true:
        game_state.roc_doctrinal_state = "institutionalized_asymmetric"
        game_state.doctrinal_reversal_path = "explicit_counter_authorship_only"

# ── P12. roc_special_budget_release_rate :: deterministic_gated ────────────
# Deterministic gate. Source [#19] (promulgation) + [#15]
# (tranche structure). Tranche 1 (NT$300B) release rate = 1.0
# unconditionally. Tranche 2 (NT$480B) release rate is binary on
# US-FMS-LOA-Round-2 issuance. Couples DIRECTLY to P12-bis below.
MATCH (t:ROC_Special_Budget_Tranche {budget_id: "NT$780B"}):
    IF t.tranche_number == 1:
        t.release_rate = 1.0
        t.gate = "unconditional"
    ELIF t.tranche_number == 2:
        IF game_state.us_exec_fms_loa_round_2_issued == true:
            t.release_rate = 1.0
        ELSE:
            t.release_rate = 0.0
        t.gate = "us_fms_loa_round_2"

# ── P12-bis. us_exec_fms_loa_cadence(t) [CROSS-PLAYER PROMOTION] ───────────
# Day-7 S8 modeled US_Exec as a single-action node
# (extend_security_umbrella ∈ {yes, no}). Day-8 S4 evidence forces
# promotion to a multi-action node with at least one continuous-control
# parameter — the FMS-LOA issuance cadence. The same US_Exec node now
# gates BOTH extended deterrence (kinetic) and Taipei's ratified-but-
# pending defense-spend (procurement). Source [#14, #15, #19, #20].
MATCH (u:Player {name: "US_Exec"}):
    u.action_nodes = [
        "extend_security_umbrella",
        "fms_loa_cadence"
    ]
    LET cadence = u.fms_loa_issuances_per_quarter
    LET fms_loa_round_2_status = u.fms_loa_round_2_issued
    u.continuous_control_parameter = "fms_loa_cadence"
    SUBMIT_INTENT "evaluate_fms_cadence" ON u WITH {window: "rolling_4_quarters"}

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# S5 — Resilience substrate predicates [#22, #23, #24, #25, #26]
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ── P13. roc_energy_buffer_days(commodity) ─────────────────────────────────
# Deterministic, time-indexed. Source [#25] NDC (actuals); [#24] MOEA
# (NG policy trajectory). The MIN across commodities sets the lower
# bound on the time-compression window any non-kinetic coercion
# campaign must work within before energy-substrate degradation
# becomes observable. NG is the binding constraint (10.7 → 14 by 2027).
MATCH (b:ROC_Energy_Buffer):
    IF b.commodity == "petroleum":
        b.days = 148
    ELIF b.commodity == "natural_gas":
        IF NOW() < duration("2027-01-01T00:00:00Z"):
            b.days = 10.7
        ELSE:
            b.days = 14
    ELIF b.commodity == "coal":
        b.days = 45.7
    # q8(A) hoist: MIN(b.days FOR b IN game_state.roc_energy_buffers)
    # aggregator-over-comprehension not in gsl_ops.lark v1.2 (Finding 5,
    # parse-verify-2026-05-16). NG is always the binding minimum across
    # {petroleum 148, NG 10.7|14, coal 45.7}; hard-coded with the
    # 2027-01-01 NG-policy step. Adding a new commodity buffer requires
    # updating this binding. Grammar-extension tracked as q9.
    IF NOW() < duration("2027-01-01T00:00:00Z"):
        game_state.coercion_window_lower_bound_days = 10.7
    ELSE:
        game_state.coercion_window_lower_bound_days = 14

# ── P14. roc_cable_resilience_response_time(t) :: monotonically-improving ─
# Stochastic with deterministic shell. 2023-Feb baseline ≈ weeks
# (720 hours order). 2026-04-30 actual response ≈ hours (Matsu-3
# microwave backup activated within hours). Source [#22]. Architecture
# hedge: Astranis dedicated-satellite track scheduled end-2026 [#26].
# Encodes: the cable-cut coercion lever has been materially loosened;
# the residual extreme-case hedge (full cable + microwave saturation)
# is the satellite path. Monotonically-decreasing-mean property is
# stochastic at the per-incident granularity; see STOCHASTIC block.
MATCH (c:ROC_Cable_Response):
    IF c.year == 2023:
        c.response_time_hours = 720
    ELIF c.year == 2026:
        c.response_time_hours = 6
    IF c.architecture_includes_dedicated_sat and NOW() >= duration("2026-12-01T00:00:00Z"):
        c.response_time_hours = MIN(c.response_time_hours, 4)
    game_state.cable_coercion_lever_state = "materially_loosened_since_2023"

# ── P15. roc_executive_energy_doctrine_layer_active ────────────────────────
# Deterministic since 2026-03. Source [#23]. Lai nuclear-restart pivot
# at Kuo-sheng and Maanshan extends the deterrence-doctrine substrate
# set from three layers (political-constitutional, rhetorical baseline,
# defense-architectural) to four (adds energy-security). Two cross-
# section implications: (a) KMT cross-strait-friendly energy-framing
# pre-empted; (b) measurable observable in restart-procedure progress.
MATCH (d:Lai_Speech_Act_Layer):
    IF d.layer_index == 4 and d.substrate == "energy_security":
        IF d.active_since >= "2026-03-01":
            game_state.roc_doctrinal_layer_count = 4
            game_state.deterrence_doctrine_substrates = [
                "political_constitutional",
                "rhetorical_baseline",
                "defense_architectural",
                "energy_security"
            ]
            game_state.kmt_cross_strait_energy_framing_preempted = true
            game_state.energy_substrate_observable = "kuo_sheng_and_maanshan_restart_progress"

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Aggregator — Day-8 ROC-player composite state
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# Daily roll-up combining the 15 above predicates into the ROC-player
# composite state node consumed by the equilibrium-tilt aggregator
# from Day-7 S8.
EVERY "P1D":
    LET p1 = game_state.roc_sovereignty_position == "non_subordinate_to_PRC"
    LET p2 = game_state.dpp_seat_share < 0.5
    LET p3 = game_state.roc_threat_perception_state == "escalating"
    LET p4 = game_state.kmt_doctrinal_alignment_active
    LET p7 = game_state.identity_is_decision_variable == false
    LET p11 = game_state.roc_doctrinal_state == "institutionalized_asymmetric"
    LET p15 = game_state.roc_doctrinal_layer_count == 4
    IF p1 and p2 and p3 and p4 and p7 and p11 and p15:
        game_state.roc_composite = "doctrinally_locked_legislatively_gated_resilience_layered"
        ALERT "Day-8 ROC composite state stable" ON game_state

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Game-tree pruning under the Day-8 ROC predicates (deterministic)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# Three Day-8 prunings (additive to Day-7 S8's five):
#
#   (D8.1) PRC strategic-redirection of cross-strait energy framing
#          via "peaceful-reunification" inducement: BLOCKED by P15's
#          energy-substrate doctrinal layer + the 2026-03 MOEA
#          rejection [#23]. The branch was a live PRC option in
#          early 2026; the Lai pivot pre-empted it.
#
#   (D8.2) ROC-Exec unilateral release of NT$480B Tranche 2 in
#          advance of US-FMS-LOA-Round-2: BLOCKED by P12's
#          deterministic gate. Tranche 2 is structurally inaccessible
#          to ROC-Exec discretion without a US_Exec action.
#
#   (D8.3) KMT-internal repudiation of 92-consensus alignment under
#          current chair: BLOCKED by P4's repudiation path requirement
#          (new chair election or formal Joint-Declarations withdrawal).
#          The branch is reachable but requires a discrete party-level
#          event, not a parliamentary maneuver.
#
# Branches that remain in the stochastic resolution set (added to
# Day-7 S8's three): the ROC-Leg factional-balance evolution under
# P5 (caucus-discipline events; chair transitions); the per-incident
# cable response-time tail under P14; the recovery trajectory of
# the TPOF war-likelihood time-series that promotes (or fails to
# promote) P9-bis to deterministic-multi-wave.

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# P28 — Substrate-discriminating Tier-3 floor predicate family
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# Emerged Day-13 (candidate) -> Day-14 (active, 3 substrates) ->
# Day-17 (7 substrates, 3 lambda-classes). Day-18 consolidation.
#
# Each P28(c) evaluates whether substrate c admits Tier-3
# status-narrowing instruments that survive without producing a
# bilateral crisis. The predicate is tier-indexed: the VALUE of
# the highest admitted tier is itself a substrate property.
#
# Parameters:
#   c = substrate identifier (EU, JPN, PHL, UK, AUS, CAN, US)
#   t = tier being tested (1, 2, 3)
#   lambda = lexical-class (A, B, C, na)
#   kappa = commission presence (present, absent)
#
# Ceiling ordinal:
#   0 = architectural absence (no Tier-3 register)
#   1 = committee report / committee discussion
#   2 = EP plenary vote (supermajority, non-binding)
#   3 = 1st reading (House) / 2nd reading (Senate)
#   4 = enacted law (multiple statutes)
#
# lambda -> ceiling mapping (N=4, observed, not causal):
#   A (collapsed)  -> ceiling in {1}       (committee)
#   B (preserved)  -> ceiling in {3}       (reading)
#   C (dual)       -> ceiling in {4}       (enacted law)
#   na             -> ceiling in {0, 1, 2} (substrate-specific)

# -- P28.setup: substrate parameter declarations -------------------------

MATCH (s:Substrate {id: "EU"}):
    game_state.p28_eu_lambda = "na"
    game_state.p28_eu_kappa = "absent"
    game_state.p28_eu_ceiling = 2
    game_state.p28_eu_result = "pass"

MATCH (s:Substrate {id: "JPN"}):
    game_state.p28_jpn_lambda = "na"
    game_state.p28_jpn_kappa = "absent"
    game_state.p28_jpn_ceiling = 1
    game_state.p28_jpn_result = "pass"

MATCH (s:Substrate {id: "PHL"}):
    game_state.p28_phl_lambda = "na"
    game_state.p28_phl_kappa = "absent"
    game_state.p28_phl_ceiling = 0
    game_state.p28_phl_result = "arch_absence"

MATCH (s:Substrate {id: "UK"}):
    game_state.p28_uk_lambda = "A"
    game_state.p28_uk_kappa = "absent"
    game_state.p28_uk_ceiling = 1
    game_state.p28_uk_result = "pass"

MATCH (s:Substrate {id: "AUS"}):
    game_state.p28_aus_lambda = "A"
    game_state.p28_aus_kappa = "absent"
    game_state.p28_aus_ceiling = 1
    game_state.p28_aus_result = "pass"

MATCH (s:Substrate {id: "CAN"}):
    game_state.p28_can_lambda = "B"
    game_state.p28_can_kappa = "present"
    game_state.p28_can_ceiling = 3
    game_state.p28_can_result = "pass_qualified"

MATCH (s:Substrate {id: "US"}):
    game_state.p28_us_lambda = "C"
    game_state.p28_us_kappa = "absent"
    game_state.p28_us_ceiling = 4
    game_state.p28_us_result = "pass"
    game_state.p28_us_d1_verb = "renshi_dao"
    game_state.p28_us_d2_verb = "chengren"
    game_state.p28_us_legislative_floor = "TRA_1979"

# -- P28.test: generic three-condition evaluation -------------------------

MATCH (c:Substrate_Test {predicate: "P28", substrate: s.id}):
    IF c.constitutional_grounding == true and c.executive_independence == true and c.non_crisis_deviation == true:
        game_state.p28_consolidated_pass_count = game_state.p28_consolidated_pass_count + 1
        LOG "P28 PASS on substrate" LEVEL "info"
    IF c.constitutional_grounding == true and c.executive_independence == true and c.non_crisis_deviation == false:
        game_state.p28_consolidated_fail_count = game_state.p28_consolidated_fail_count + 1
        LOG "P28 FAIL on substrate (crisis-producing)" LEVEL "warn"
    IF c.constitutional_grounding == false:
        game_state.p28_arch_absence_count = game_state.p28_arch_absence_count + 1
        LOG "P28 ARCH-ABSENCE on substrate" LEVEL "info"

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Day-21 (2026-05-30) — Nexus-binding predicates P29 + P30
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# Day-21 is the first Nexus-implication publication in the series. Two new
# deterministic predicates land here:
#
#   P29 — per-substrate Nexus binding via ChipExposure threshold.
#         Static structural property: market-cap(primary_chip_ticker) / GDP(s)
#         exceeds 0.05 → chip-supply-chain Nexus binding present.
#
#   P30 — coupling-property → market correlation under direct-cross-strait
#         stress conditioning. Day-21 H21.1 test verdict = INCONCLUSIVE (2/4)
#         against pre-committed rule (filed at silicon-strait commit 134b09b
#         §2.2 and bridge commit 5388040 §3.2). Refinement-hypothesis H21.1a/b
#         encoded below for forward Day-22+ testing.
#
# Pre-registration anchors for P29 + P30:
#   - bridge commit 5388040 (Day-20 cron-C, 2026-05-29 14:00 CEST) §6.1
#   - cron-A scoping commit 134b09b (Day-21 cron-A, 2026-05-30 06:00 CEST) §2.5
#
# Parse-status: both predicates hoisted-flat form per Day-9 q8(A) path; should
# parse cleanly against gsl_ops.lark v1.2 deterministic subset. Parse-verify
# queued for Day-22 cron-A per Day-9 cadence (research/audit/parse-verify-*).
#
# Both predicates assume substrate primary_chip_exposure_ticker is defined
# via prior MATCH (s:Substrate) population (see P28-block substrate inventory).

# -- P29 — per-substrate Nexus binding (deterministic) -------------------

MATCH (s:Substrate {id: <substrate_id>}):
    game_state.p29_substrate         = s.id
    game_state.p29_primary_ticker    = s.primary_chip_exposure_ticker
    game_state.p29_market_cap        = s.market_cap_primary_ticker
    game_state.p29_gdp               = s.substrate_gdp
    game_state.p29_chip_exposure     = s.market_cap_primary_ticker / s.substrate_gdp
    game_state.p29_nexus_binding     = (s.market_cap_primary_ticker / s.substrate_gdp) > 0.05

# -- P29.test: nexus-binding evaluation ----------------------------------

MATCH (c:Substrate_Test {predicate: "P29", substrate: s.id}):
    IF c.p29_nexus_binding == true:
        game_state.p29_nexus_binding_count = game_state.p29_nexus_binding_count + 1
        LOG "P29 PASS on substrate (chip-supply-chain Nexus binding present)" LEVEL "info"
    IF c.p29_nexus_binding == false:
        game_state.p29_no_binding_count = game_state.p29_no_binding_count + 1
        LOG "P29 NO-BINDING on substrate (no first-order chip-supply-chain Nexus binding)" LEVEL "info"

# Reference instantiations (8-substrate corpus, indicative — values to be
# audited in cron-D Nisaba pass and updated per primary-source pull):
#
#   TWN: ChipExposure ≈ 1.5–2.0 (TSMC market_cap / TWN GDP); P29 PASS
#   ROK: ChipExposure ≈ 0.5–0.6 (Samsung + SK Hynix combined / ROK GDP); P29 PASS
#   JPN: ChipExposure(Toyota proxy) << 0.05; P29 NO-BINDING in single-ticker form
#        — JPN binding routes via Advantest + collected semis-equipment ticker basket
#   US:  ChipExposure(NVDA) ≈ 0.03; P29 NO-BINDING at single-ticker threshold
#        — US binding routes via SOX sector aggregation
#   EU:  ChipExposure(ASML proxy) ≈ 0.02; P29 NO-BINDING single-ticker
#        — EU binding routes via Chip Act 43B EUR macro-channel
#   PRC: ChipExposure(SMIC) < 0.01; P29 NO-BINDING (structural under-development of
#        bleeding-edge fab capacity captured by threshold)

# -- P30 — coupling-property → market correlation (deterministic, falsifiable)

MATCH (s:Substrate {id: <substrate_id>}):
    game_state.p30_substrate                = s.id
    game_state.p30_coupling_property        = s.coupling_property
    game_state.p30_primary_ticker           = s.primary_chip_exposure_ticker
    game_state.p30_corr_stress              = s.corr_primary_ticker_TSM_stress_event_median
    game_state.p30_corr_baseline            = s.corr_primary_ticker_TSM_baseline_median
    game_state.p30_delta                    = s.corr_primary_ticker_TSM_stress_event_median - s.corr_primary_ticker_TSM_baseline_median
    game_state.p30_event_class              = s.stress_event_class
    game_state.p30_predicted_elevation      = (s.coupling_property == true) and (s.stress_event_class == "direct_cross_strait")

# -- P30.test: H21.1a / H21.1b evaluation --------------------------------

MATCH (c:Substrate_Test {predicate: "P30", substrate: s.id, event: e.id}):
    IF c.p30_predicted_elevation == true and c.p30_delta > 0.10:
        game_state.p30_h21_1a_pass_count = game_state.p30_h21_1a_pass_count + 1
        LOG "P30 PASS — coupling + direct-cross-strait + delta>0.10 (H21.1a confirmed)" LEVEL "info"
    IF c.p30_predicted_elevation == true and c.p30_delta <= 0.10:
        game_state.p30_h21_1a_fail_count = game_state.p30_h21_1a_fail_count + 1
        LOG "P30 FAIL — coupling + direct-cross-strait but delta<=0.10 (H21.1a falsified at event)" LEVEL "warn"
    IF c.p30_predicted_elevation == false and abs(c.p30_delta) < 0.10:
        game_state.p30_h21_1b_pass_count = game_state.p30_h21_1b_pass_count + 1
        LOG "P30 PASS — non-elevation predicted and |delta|<0.10 (H21.1b confirmed)" LEVEL "info"
    IF c.p30_predicted_elevation == false and abs(c.p30_delta) >= 0.10:
        game_state.p30_h21_1b_fail_count = game_state.p30_h21_1b_fail_count + 1
        LOG "P30 FAIL — non-elevation predicted but |delta|>=0.10 (H21.1b falsified at event)" LEVEL "warn"

# Day-21 H21.1 test data (cron-C commit 5abc425, falsification verdict INCONCLUSIVE
# at 2/4 against pre-committed rule filed at commits 134b09b and 5388040):
#
#   ROK 005930.KS ↔ TSM @ PEL_2022 (direct-cross-strait):   delta=+0.252 → P30 PASS (H21.1a)
#   ROK 005930.KS ↔ TSM @ DUV_2023 (semis-policy):          delta=-0.046 → P30 PASS (H21.1b)
#   ROK 005930.KS ↔ TSM @ LAI_2024 (symbolic-political):    delta=-0.033 → P30 PASS (H21.1b)
#   ROK 005930.KS ↔ TSM @ PRC_2025 (direct-cross-strait):   delta=+0.411 → P30 PASS (H21.1a)
#
# At P30 level (refined H21.1a + H21.1b), all 4 events pass. The verdict
# difference between H21.1 (INCONCLUSIVE) and P30 (4/4 PASS post-refinement)
# is the structural point: the refined hypothesis pair fits the data, but
# the refinement was filed AFTER the pre-committed test ran, so per
# pre-registration discipline (skill §invariants + Day-19/20 P28 audit
# precedent), Day-21 reports H21.1 INCONCLUSIVE as the verdict and files
# H21.1a/b for Day-22+ blind testing. P30 here encodes the refined predicate
# for forward audit cycles, not as a Day-21 re-derivation.

